84
00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.000
I think it's actually slightly overfitting things to a simplistic model.

85
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.600
But like it's a nice way of looking at things.

86
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:58.000
Um, and then the civil war, the English Civil War, you have this, the mercantile side effectively wins, takes over, but then tries to set up its own hereditary system.

87
00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:06.880
Everyone decides to restore the king, king comes back, Charles II, son of Charles I, who was executed um at the beginning of the English Civil War.

88
00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:38.800
Um, then when he tries to hand over to, sorry, when he he hands over to James I, but when he has tries to hand over to James II, who is an open Catholic, then the same mercantile elites are worried, we're going back to absolutism, we're going back to rule by the aristocratic uh elites, and we we're not gonna have the um the system of I guess like mercantile freedom that they wanted, but lots of other stuff is wrapped up in that, like different kinds of Christianity and so on.

89
00:08:38.800 --> 00:09:06.280
And so they invite in the ruler of the Netherlands, the ruler of Holland, well, they would have said Holland at the time, William, who happens to be married to the daughter of the English king, um, and they they invade in Devon in southwest England, and pretty much normal it's a deliberately broad model, but it links technological progress to who holds political power.

